<title>SPAIN: Cepsa says buys Atlas lubricants firm.</title>
<headline>Cepsa says buys Atlas lubricants firm.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish energy group Cepsa said on Friday it had bought 100 percent of Atlas Combustibles y Lubricantes from Distribuidora Industrial (DISA).</p>
<p>Cepsa did not specify a price.</p>
<p>Atlas operates in Ceuta and Melilla and has two LPG packaging plants and six service stations. Annual sales are around 25 million litres of gasoline and gasoil at its service stations, and its LPG factories distribute around 6,000 tonnes of butane and propane.</p>
<p>Cepsa said the incorporation of Atlas represented further progress in increasing its sales network.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
